From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrummingBird1 <1979036+DrummingBird1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:29:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] D3D12: internal resolution (D3D12_RES_SCALE)

D3D12_RES_SCALE=1..4 renders every guest surface at that multiple of its
size: the frame, the offscreen colour and depth surfaces, the shared depth
buffer and the screen copy. Surfaces keep their guest size in w/h and draw
records stay in guest pixels; only the D3D12 resources and the pixel
rectangles given to the rasterizer and to copies are scaled (rs_px,
rs_set_rect), so both edges of a rectangle scale and neighbours still meet.
The present pass samples the larger frame, and the setting needs it.

A surface's first upload from guest memory is stretched by nearest texel in
ordinary memory and written to the upload heap in order: stretching in the
write-combined heap itself took 6 s for one 2048x2048 surface at x3.
Those upload buffers are now released at the start of the next frame
instead of living as long as the surface. Fragment programs that read WPOS
get it divided back into guest pixels. Frame dumps and captures read the
scaled size. RT_CREATE_DBG=<n> logs surface creations with their cost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
